.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel - Manage durable tunnels or start an ephemeral tunnel


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel [--ephemeral] [<port|url|path>] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage durable tunnels, or start a temporary preview. A durable tunnel keeps its address,
routes, domains and access rules across sessions and restarts; manage it with create, list,
show, route, domain, policy, pause, resume and delete. pb tunnel with no subcommand prints help.

.PP
With --ephemeral and a target (a port, URL or path) the command behaves exactly like pb preview:
a temporary preview with its own lifecycle. pb tunnel stop stops only previews; a durable tunnel
is paused or deleted.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--background\fP[=false]
	hand the preview to this computer's background service and return once ready (default lifetime 30m)

.PP
\fB--domain\fP=[]
	attach a verified custom domain (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tunnel

.PP
\fB--host-header\fP=""
	send this Host to the origin instead of the public host (http, https, h2c targets; for dev servers with a host allow-list)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the canonical preview resource as JSON

.PP
\fB--private\fP[=false]
	limit the preview to this account

.PP
\fB--team\fP[=false]
	require an explicit team grant for browser access

.PP
\fB--ttl\fP=0s
	bounded preview lifetime (maximum 24h)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel create web --port 8080
  pb tunnel list
  pb tunnel --ephemeral 3000 --private
  pb tunnel stop preview_abc123
.EE


